            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130"
            },
            "displayName": "Jukka Zitting",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "Do we expect the JSON query format to be widely used (i.e. by more clients than the object model) with the UserManager API? In that case I'd simply support it directly in the API by exposing a findAuthorizables(String query) method.\n\nOtherwise, if we don't expect the JSON format to be widely used, is the jcr-commons component then the right place for this code?\n",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=jukkaz",
            "name": "jukkaz",
            "key": "jukkaz",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130"
            },
            "displayName": "Jukka Zitting",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "created": "2011-08-18T10:09:05.307+0000",
          "updated": "2011-08-18T10:09:05.307+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12519262/comment/13086932",
          "id": "13086932",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=mduerig",
            "name": "mduerig",
            "key": "mduerig",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=mduerig&avatarId=13834",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=mduerig&avatarId=13834",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=mduerig&avatarId=13834",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=mduerig&avatarId=13834"
            },
            "displayName": "Michael D\u00fcrig",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Bucharest"
          },
          "body": "So the question is whether to add findAuthorizables(String query) to the API and put the code into jackrabbit-core or to put the code somewhere else (i.e jcr-commons). I'd go for the second since it seems more modular to me. If it turns out (which I doubt) that there is really a need for a findAuthorizables(String query) method in the API we can still add that later on. ",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=mduerig",
            "name": "mduerig",
            "key": "mduerig",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=mduerig&avatarId=13834",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=mduerig&avatarId=13834",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=mduerig&avatarId=13834",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=mduerig&avatarId=13834"
            },
            "displayName": "Michael D\u00fcrig",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Bucharest"
          },
          "created": "2011-08-18T10:17:56.996+0000",
          "updated": "2011-08-18T10:17:56.996+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12519262/comment/13086941",
          "id": "13086941",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=jukkaz",
            "name": "jukkaz",
            "key": "jukkaz",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130"
            },
            "displayName": "Jukka Zitting",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "Fair point. I'm just trying to establish how important and/or widely used this feature (JSON query format) is and how many clients really are using it. This sounds rather like a specific integration scenario (i.e. a single backend servlet for Ajax clients) than a generic use case, especially since we already do have the query builder API for Java clients. I'm therefore a bit reluctant to have this in jcr-commons.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=jukkaz",
            "name": "jukkaz",
            "key": "jukkaz",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130"
            },
            "displayName": "Jukka Zitting",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "created": "2011-08-18T10:40:00.666+0000",
          "updated": "2011-08-18T10:40:00.666+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12519262/comment/13086943",
          "id": "13086943",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=mduerig",
            "name": "mduerig",
            "key": "mduerig",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=mduerig&avatarId=13834",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=mduerig&avatarId=13834",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=mduerig&avatarId=13834",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=mduerig&avatarId=13834"
            },
            "displayName": "Michael D\u00fcrig",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Bucharest"
          },
          "body": "What other options are there? It seems a bit alien for jackrabbit-core. Putting it directly into jackrabbit-api doesn't seem right to me.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=mduerig",
            "name": "mduerig",
            "key": "mduerig",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=mduerig&avatarId=13834",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=mduerig&avatarId=13834",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=mduerig&avatarId=13834",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=mduerig&avatarId=13834"
            },
            "displayName": "Michael D\u00fcrig",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Bucharest"
          },
          "created": "2011-08-18T10:47:44.854+0000",
          "updated": "2011-08-18T10:47:44.854+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12519262/comment/13086946",
          "id": "13086946",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=jukkaz",
            "name": "jukkaz",
            "key": "jukkaz",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130"
            },
            "displayName": "Jukka Zitting",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "Why do we need it in Jackrabbit? Assuming the purpose of this code is to support Ajax clients, the code should simply reside with the servlet that processes requests sent by those clients.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=jukkaz",
            "name": "jukkaz",
            "key": "jukkaz",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130"
            },
            "displayName": "Jukka Zitting",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "created": "2011-08-18T10:52:03.857+0000",
          "updated": "2011-08-18T10:52:03.857+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12519262/comment/13086947",
          "id": "13086947",
          "author": {
